<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kimpa Vita</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1684–1706</span> · Also known as Beatriz Kimpa Vita, Dona Beatriz</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kimpa Vita, baptised Beatriz, was a Kongolese prophet who founded the Antonian movement during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-kongo">Kongo</a> civil wars. In 1704 she claimed to be possessed by Saint Anthony, taught that Christ and the saints were Kongolese, and called for the kingdom to be reunited under a king at the ruined capital São <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salvador">Salvador</a>. Her followers reoccupied the city, but she was captured and burnt as a heretic on the orders of Pedro IV in 1706.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kimpa-vita.jpg" alt="Kimpa Vita" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Somebody040404 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kimpa_Vita_%C2%B4s_statue_in_Angola.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
